WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.150
Hey David, I'm curious, have you ever asked
to speak to the manager?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.690
Are you one of those guys?

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:07.550
Uh, barely ever.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:13.830
There are very, very few circumstances where
I have had to a lobby, a sort of a complaint

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.870
of some kind.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:21.409
Uh, and when I do, I am really, really, really
polite partially because, um, it's happening

00:00:21.409 --> 00:00:25.679
more and more that like, I'll go to a restaurant
and then when I'm leaving the restaurant,

00:00:25.679 --> 00:00:28.470
someone will come up to me and say, hey, didn't
want to bother you while you were eating,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.229
but love the show.

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:35.890
And it would be so embarrassing if I threw
a fit to a manager, uh, at a restaurant and

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.920
a viewer side and was horrified by it.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.760
But in all seriousness, when I've had to lobby
a complaint, it's most often been either dealing

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.180
with airlines or dealing with hotels.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.170
Those are the most common times that something
was truly wrong.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:54.210
You know, a shower that, uh, leaked all over
the bathroom floor.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.870
Okay, well that, that's gotta be dealt with.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:03.070
Um, you know, I the, these are relatively
limited incidents, but when something like

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:10.429
that happens, I am always very polite to people
who are working often underpaid in a variety

00:01:10.429 --> 00:01:11.640
of different jobs.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:17.369
And one of the most cringe inducing things
for me socially is when I go out, it happens

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:18.640
most frequently at restaurants.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.729
I go out to restaurants with people usually
that I don't know that well because I like

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:27.179
to think I don't closely associate with people
who treat wait staff poorly and someone starts

00:01:27.179 --> 00:01:28.670
being rude to the wait staff.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:34.159
It is a, an immediate red flag if that's how
you're treating in front of people you barely

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:35.549
know in public.

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:40.869
This is how you're treating people who are
underpaid, working in what are often not the

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:44.139
best environments depending on where it is
that they work and you're treating them like

00:01:44.139 --> 00:01:45.139
that.

00:01:45.139 --> 00:01:46.439
You're not someone I want to be friends with.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.770
You're not someone I want to do business with.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.979
You're not someone I really want to be spending
time with.

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:52.310
So I do sometimes ask to speak to the manager.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.979
Uh, and I'm always extremely polite when I
do it.

00:01:55.979 --> 00:02:01.950
Trying to think of the last time I had to
do something like, hey, it was just a bad

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:02.950
hotel.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.020
I think it was, um, where was I?

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:10.500
I think it was when I was last in Montreal
a few months ago, there was a, the plumbing

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:16.530
stopped working multiple times at the hotel
and eventually I asked them, it wasn't like

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.780
a room issue.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:22.930
I said, you know, I need to be able to get
in the shower and, and flush the toilet.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:27.630
Um, I'm gonna need you to transfer us to a
different hotel and sort of like take care

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:28.990
of the arrangements.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:30.941
Um, and they did and that was it.

00:02:30.941 --> 00:02:32.380
And they apologized.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.860
And a nobody, nobody was embarrassed or shamed
by me.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.780
I just said, this is what we gotta do.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:40.560
Uh, please treat everybody with kindness and
respect.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.650
That's my, uh, that's my sign off today.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:45.730
If you have a question you want answered,
let me know.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.230
Ideally via email.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:52.570
That's the most sort of personal and professional
way to let me know that you have a question

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.770
you want answered.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.480
Use the contact usPage@davidpacman.com.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.830
Great Bonus show for you today.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.890
Coming up next if you are a member or a friend.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.299
Otherwise, I will talk to you on Monday

